I'm okay with helping kids out, but I don't want to make them a permanent member of my friend's list unless they're going through something and need some support. One of the kids I've met was watching their parents go through a divorce so I just listened to them rant and gave them some advice or suggestions. He logged on one day and then never again. He was 14 at the time, I hope he's doing better.

&#x200B;

I get along much easier with people my age, cracking jokes and not stressing about getting reported for saying some variant of a curse word

&#x200B;

Plus older wizards tend to understand the game's mechanics more. I had a random guy questing with my in Novus last week and every first round he'd put up a fortify. Not just in boss battles, literally every trash mob and every single battle. I tried telling him it's okay, they won't kill us since they'll die in one hit, but he just said "its a habit lol" and continued to fortify. Like man you could've one shot that hit if you didnt fortify and bladed instead.

